; Header #R targets are layout statement starts that build each camera
; window. $E6DB walks from #R$8B69 through #R$9207 by room pass and camera.

[Room:#N$00]
#HTML(
<table>
  <tr><th>Room #N$00 Patio at #R$A839</th></tr>
  <tr>
    <td>#ROOM$00,$20,$40</td>
  </tr>
</table>
)

[Room:#N$01]
#HTML(
<table>
  <tr><th>Room #N$01 Storage Cupboard at #R$A2A8</th></tr>
  <tr>
    <td>
      Scenery layout for room #N$01 in #R$8B69. Floor strips continue at
      #R$A2F1. Shelves use #R$A6BB.
    </td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>#ROOM$01,$40,$60</td>
  </tr>
</table>
)

[Room:#N$02]
#HTML(
<table>
  <tr><th>Room #N$02 Mid camera stove band at #R$9FDC</th></tr>
  <tr>
    <td>
      Room #N$02 is not a separate room. It is the room number on the
      stove, hatch and trap floor entries, which are drawn in an
      in-between camera window from #N$6C to #N$8C spanning Trap Door and
      Kitchen. Lit stove layout #R$9FDC. Closed hatch #R$A3F3 and trap
      floor #R$A453 share this band.
    </td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>#ROOM$02,$6C,$8C</td>
  </tr>
</table>
)

[Room:#N$03]
#HTML(
<table>
  <tr><th>Room #N$03 Trap Door at #R$A3F3</th></tr>
  <tr>
    <td>
      Closed hatch layout. Wall scenery in this window is #R$A237.
    </td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>#ROOM$03,$60,$80</td>
  </tr>
</table>
)

[Room:#N$04]
#HTML(
<table>
  <tr><th>Room #N$04 Kitchen at #R$9FDC</th></tr>
  <tr>
    <td>
      Lit stove in this camera. Also the dumb waiter #R$A7DA and lever
      scenery #R$A827.
    </td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>#ROOM$04,$80,$A0</td>
  </tr>
</table>
)

[Room:#N$05]
#HTML(
<table>
  <tr><th>Room #N$05 Weight at #R$A61C</th></tr>
  <tr>
    <td>
      Vertical columns under #R$90B7 (room #N$05). White arch into the
      Swamp is #R$A508 at #R$917B.
    </td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>#ROOM$05,$A0,$C0</td>
  </tr>
</table>
)

[Room:Swamp]
#HTML(
<table>
  <tr><th>Swamp (camera #N$E0 to #N$FF) at #R$A929</th></tr>
  <tr>
    <td>
      Dripping water wrap scenery (room #N$00 high X in #R$8B69).
      Waterline strips also use #R$AA28.
    </td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>#ROOM$06,$E0,$FF</td>
  </tr>
</table>
)
